On 23/05/07, a couple of people wrote:

> I wouldn't worry about phonological distortion, if I were you.

Of course if it is particularly important that the pronunciation is
exactly right, you could use {la'o}, which imports a phrase from
another language with no modification at all:

.i mi finti sepi'o la'o gy. LaTeX .gy.
.i mi tcidu nelci la'o gy. xkcd .gy. vau zo'o


